<pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I87c7508358f3912016afb2faf5b2233adbcfcce1" commit="9e00b2c6d0c781716f62ed18ed4ad0ce85250570" commit_message="login: Notify Chrome of container exit  This change adds a callback to StartContainer() that will be invoked when the container terminates and wires it up to send a D-Bus notification that Chrome can observe.  BUG=b:29190864 TEST=kill -9 $container_pid  # Chrome receives D-Bus notification. TEST=StopArcInstance()  # Chrome still receives D-Bus notification.  Change-Id: I87c7508358f3912016afb2faf5b2233adbcfcce1 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/351630 Commit-Ready: Luis Hector Chavez &lt;lhchavez@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Luis Hector Chavez &lt;lhchavez@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Dan Erat &lt;derat@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="3" gerrit_number="351630" owner_email="lhchavez@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="8" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/30/351630/8" remote="cros" total_fail_count="3"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I2928a0bfe4e9d46e6e826b075c05e659c7c1160e" commit="4b83c8ebec9408db1ac21535822792bc82aea200" commit_message="login: Support a custom command for container termination  Given that containers will typically run an init process and those usually don't receive any signals (except for SIGKILL), it makes sense to allow for a subclass of ContainerManagerImpl to define its own termination logic. In particular, the Android container does need to enter the container namespaces and run a command to signal clean termination.  BUG=b:29179661 TEST=Android still shuts down cleanly CQ-DEPEND=CL:*264538,CL:351630  Change-Id: I2928a0bfe4e9d46e6e826b075c05e659c7c1160e Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/352352 Commit-Ready: Luis Hector Chavez &lt;lhchavez@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Luis Hector Chavez &lt;lhchavez@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Mattias Nissler &lt;mnissler@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Dan Erat &lt;derat@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="3" gerrit_number="352352" owner_email="lhchavez@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="9" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/52/352352/9" remote="cros" total_fail_count="3"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.14" change_id="Ib9d8b5b3254028124bbdc409f7ba1d9f02c20001" commit="577d248c4a151fcaa8d5df6a019724ae69bc8f71" commit_message="FROMLIST: net: Allow xt_owner in any user namespace  Making this work is a little tricky as it really isn't kosher to change the xt_owner_match_info in a check function.  Without changing xt_owner_match_info we need to know the user namespace the uids and gids are specified in.  In the common case net-&gt;user_ns == current_user_ns().  Verify net-&gt;user_ns == current_user_ns() in owner_check so we can later assume it in owner_mt.  In owner_check also verify that all of the uids and gids specified are in net-&gt;user_ns and that the expected min/max relationship exists between the uids and gids in xt_owner_match_info.  In owner_mt get the network namespace from the outgoing socket, as this must be the same network namespace as the netfilter rules, and use that network namespace to find the user namespace the uids and gids in xt_match_owner_info are encoded in.  Then convert from their encoded from into the kernel internal format for uids and gids and perform the owner match.  BUG=b:29161036 TEST=`/system/bin/iptables -w -A fw_dozable -m owner --uid-owner 0 -j RETURN`      run from android-sh root shell  Link: https://lists.linuxfoundation.org/pipermail/containers/2014-May/034514.html Signed-off-by: &quot;Eric W. Biederman&quot; &lt;ebiederm@xmission.com&gt;  Change-Id: Ib9d8b5b3254028124bbdc409f7ba1d9f02c20001 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/350510 Commit-Ready: Kevin Cernekee &lt;cernekee@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Kevin Cernekee &lt;cernekee@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Ricky Zhou &lt;rickyz@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Dylan Reid &lt;dgreid@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="2" gerrit_number="350510" owner_email="cernekee@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/10/350510/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="2"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.14" change_id="I72b1b743ae36724ae164c75cd1543fb043077fb6" commit="f9204f7d44ef15831c6a6d5afa6a4689f39b7eee" commit_message="CHROMIUM: Make ANDROID_PARANOID_NETWORK a per-netns setting  ANDROID_PARANOID_NETWORK requires creators of AF_INET/AF_INET6 sockets to be in the AID_INET group.  In our system it is problematic to enable this globally.  Change the logic so that the changes apply on a per-netns basis.  Also, interpret AID_* as gids instead of kgids.  BUG=b:27932716 TEST=`echo 1 &gt; /proc/sys/net/core/android_paranoid`  Change-Id: I72b1b743ae36724ae164c75cd1543fb043077fb6 Signed-off-by: Kevin Cernekee &lt;cernekee@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/344859 Reviewed-by: Ricky Zhou &lt;rickyz@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="344859" owner_email="cernekee@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/59/344859/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I2b9286ca3f6915ecf8e596f8f8fef27d850725e5" commit="e0509c9acd2ba6ea3e7a8993b0ba6b158e2dc055" commit_message="platform/mtpd: Add systemd service file  systemd unit file that starts the mtpd daemon BUG=chromium:583671 TEST=Checked that the mtpd daemon is up and running with   &quot;systemctl status mtpd&quot;. Plugged phone and I could browse   files. CQ-DEPEND=CL:351980 Change-Id: I2b9286ca3f6915ecf8e596f8f8fef27d850725e5 Reviewed-on: https://chro